## Summary

I shipped a production-grade, native Apple-idiomatic **`WidgetDetailCard`** widget primitive at parity with `web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/shared/WidgetDetailCard.tsx`, committed as `8bcb258ce`.

**7 files** in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/widget-primitives/` (1393 lines):
- `.Adapter.swift` — Foundation-only value types (`DetailEntry`/badge/value) + `WidgetDetailProjectionBuilder` (the pure cached→projection adapter: web empty-vs-content branch, `compact ? slice(0,4)`, `value ?? '—'`, `badgeVariantMap` error→danger).
- `.Model.swift` — `@Observable WidgetDetailCardModel` (P1/S8 state-holder + `InMemory` source), P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry seam, P1/S10 `WidgetDetailStrings` facade, a11y seam.
- `.Views.swift` — parity rows (label·value·badge), badge chip, loading/empty/error views, stale/offline banner, variant→`TSTone`.
- `.swift` — the surface (phase switch + banner, `surfaceSlug`, start/stop).
- `.Previews.swift`, `.Tests.swift` (29 tests), `.strings` (7 keys).

**Every state renders** (content, compact, empty, loading, error, stale, offline); no networking in views; no English literals; no charts/maps (the web source has none).

